rt  uh you know as a cop who's there with  his daughter liza now this is also kind  of a big change too  is it jon stewart as an ex-military guy  usually when you think of like a cop in  the green lanterns you think of guy  gardner right you don't really think of  jon stewart but it's one of these cool  little things now in the midst of this  you know as he's kind of talking to his  daughter and she's kind of like you know  everybody's staring at my crutches and  that kind of thing feeling very very uh  self-conscious about the surgery she'd  gone to the injuries she'd sustained  different things like that the reality  is jon stewart really kind of reminds us  of the version that we know from the  main dc universe  when he tells her like here's the thing  right things are different now for you  but at the end of the day remember who  you are right don't let other people get  to you at the end of the day that's  really kind of what's going on  you know don't let them bother you don't  let them get to you just kind of do your  own thing  in the middle of all that there's a kind  of a scuffle across the street  and when one of the guys is like there's  a cop over there then the person who's  doing the scuffling right the the  criminal we can call him that looks over  and realizes jon stewart and says oh no  no don't worry about him he owes my dad  right like this guy owes my dad money so  you know it's it's not a great big huge  deal at that point  jon stewart freaks out now because of  the fact that this is such a  short uh comic right three or four pages  there isn't really a whole lot given to  us in terms of extreme detail but we can  kind of fill in the blanks on our own  right that one of the things that he  talks about here is that when it comes  to the bad guys getting a hold of the  good guys and getting good guys to do  bad things  that it's not usually with like bullets  and bombs right sometimes that happens  right sometimes it happens when you know  you have have  villains criminals what have you who  just you know show up guns blazing  and just kind of spray everything down  but the reality is that in this  situation  in john's case it was that he made a  mistake that when his daughter  needed surgery that he didn't have the  money to do it on his own so he  basically ended up taking money from  what seems to be a crime boss and that  he paid him back right he did whatever  it is he needed to do and then he paid  the guy back his debts clear but the  reality is  as far as you know those members of the  criminal underworld who are familiar  with the situation go  jon stewart owes this guy right so it's  one of these things where he's kind of  tainted right and it's just gonna follow  him around or seems to follow him around  forever now  unlike jon stewart as we know him where  he's a lot more controlled he's a lot  more reserved that he's very very  methodical as opposed to being more  emotional like hal jordan right you know  quick to fly off the handle in the case  of somebody like kyle rainer where he's  he's a lot more confined in that way  here he just loses it right he  immediately starts attacking this guy  and again that's the nature of earth 3  that the characters are essentially  their opposites right as we know them in  terms of personality in terms of their  powers as far as how they get them the  role they play  in the superhero landscape and so he  just like literally starts attacking  this guy and he's like you don't control  me you don't own me  none of that stuff right nobody owns me  but at the end of the day the biggest  issue that he sees himself kind of  falling into here  is that he's kind of becoming that  villain right becoming that version of  himself that he simply didn't  necessarily want to be now  one of the things that's kind of murky  about earth 3 and it's one of the things  that dc's kind of  waxed and waned on going all the way  back to the pre-crisis days  uh you know in the the po